# Feature: Workflow & process engine

Every design moves through configurable Main Processes and Sub-processes -
never a fixed hardcoded path.

## Master data
- `DesignProcessMaster`: ProcessId, Code, Name, Sequence, Active, AppliesToProductType.
- `DesignSubProcessMaster`: SubProcessId, ProcessId, Code, Name, Sequence,
  DefaultRole, IsApproval, IsCorrectionAllowed, IsFileRequired, Active.
- `ProductProcessMapping`: ties product type to required process/sub-process.
- `WorkflowPattern` / `WorkflowPatternTask`: reusable templates, versioned
  (`VersionNo`, `Active`, `EffectiveFrom/To`), referencing `ProcessId` /
  `SubProcessId` - never storing display text only.

## Default process model
| Main Process | Default Sub-processes |
|---|---|
| Design Development | Concept Review; Sketch Creation; Sketch Approval; Punching/Wilcom; Punching Checking; Correction |
| Sample Development | Material Requirement; Fabric Issue; Machine Sample; Sample Receive; Sample Checking; Re-Sample |
| Production Release | Costing; Final Approval; Production Instruction; Production Release; Live Design Review |

## Rule
Do not hardcode employee names in workflow patterns. Store `RoleId`/`SkillId`;
resolve to an eligible employee only at task-generation time.

## API
- `GET /api/masters/processes` - process/sub-process master.
- `GET /api/workflow-patterns` - workflow pattern definitions.
